// W4d surface fold-in — `data` datatype declarations (parse-only fixture).
//
// GRADUATION: the concrete `data` surface enters the PBG grammar now
// (wyrd-ku0f) so it never needs a later re-parse; the datatype SEMANTICS —
// constructors as values, `case` elaboration, structural recursion — graduate
// under wyrd-e0xy. This `surface/` tree is PBG-only (the committed tree-sitter
// grammar does not produce these kinds) and firewalled from lowering / eval:
// the parser's zero-obligation corpus gate is the only harness that reads it.

// A nullary-only enumeration (each member is a bare uppercase constructor).
data Color { Red, Green, Blue }

// Parameterised constructors carry inline `name: Type` fields.
data Maybe(a) { None, Some(x: a) }

// Recursive datatypes need nothing new: a self-reference `Tree(a)` inside a
// field is an ordinary type application.
data Tree(a) { Leaf, Node(l: Tree(a), x: a, r: Tree(a)) }

// The empty (uninhabited) datatype. (Its name must be an ordinary
// type-identifier: `Void` is a reserved primitive-type keyword, so a datatype
// declaration uses a fresh name like `Empty`.)
data Empty {}
